// All of FreightDock's player-facing text, in English: the one place it is written (see Docs/Localization.md).
// Register (BP_Startup) adds it to the game's "en" strings, so a language mod can translate any key. T looks a key up
// in the player's language, falling back to the English here when the game has nothing for it. Placeholders in
// braces ({dock}, {n}, ...) are filled with Fill. Mod Options use the game's keys for them:
// setting.FreightDock-<option id>.name / .description (BPL_FDOptions). Modlog lines stay in code (players don't see
// them). Tools/FreightDock/text_hook.py (a Claude Code hook) lists every entry an edit here writes, for review, and
// flags text written straight into other sources.

